- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(Parser.parse(readme.stream).children.size.show)
+ Out.println(Parser.parse(readme.stream).children.size.show)

- Out.println(readme.read[Markdown of Layout].children.size.show)
+ Out.println(readme.read[Markdown of Layout].children.size.show)

= Out.println(readme.read[Markdown of Layout].children.size.show)
- ```
+ ```

- The whole CommonMark conformance suite passes through the streaming entry, a character at a
- time, so a document which is split at any point parses to the same tree as the whole text.
+ Die gesamte CommonMark-Konformitätssuite durchläuft den Streaming-Einstieg, ein Zeichen nach dem
+ anderen, sodass ein an beliebiger Stelle geteiltes Dokument zum selben Baum geparst wird wie der
+ ganze Text.

- ### Rendering to HTML
+ ### Darstellung als HTML

- `html` converts a parsed document to HTML, and `show` writes the result as text. A document
- of blocks becomes flow content, and the inline content within it becomes phrasing content,
- so the output is well-formed by construction:
+ `html` wandelt ein geparstes Dokument in HTML um, und `show` schreibt das Ergebnis als Text. Ein
+ Dokument aus Blöcken wird zu Flow-Inhalt, und der Inline-Inhalt darin zu Phrasing-Inhalt, sodass
+ die Ausgabe durch Konstruktion wohlgeformt ist:

= so the output is well-formed by construction:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= so the output is well-formed by construction:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= so the output is well-formed by construction:
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(document.html.show)
+ Out.println(document.html.show)

= Out.println(document.html.show)
- ```
+ ```

- ### The syntax tree
+ ### Der Syntaxbaum

- The `children` of a document are `Layout` nodes, and each has its inline content as `Prose`.
- A document can therefore be inspected, or transformed, by matching on the tree:
+ Die `children` eines Dokuments sind `Layout`-Knoten, und jeder hat seinen Inline-Inhalt als
+ `Prose`. Ein Dokument lässt sich daher durch Abgleich über den Baum untersuchen oder
+ transformieren:

= A document can therefore be inspected, or transformed, by matching on the tree:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val heading = document.children.head match
+ val heading = document.children.head match

-   case Layout.Heading(_, level, Prose.Textual(text)) => (level, text)
+   case Layout.Heading(_, level, Prose.Textual(text)) => (level, text)

-   case _                                             => (0, t"")
+   case _                                             => (0, t"")

=   case _                                             => (0, t"")
- ```
+ ```

=   case _                                             => (0, t"")
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

=   case _                                             => (0, t"")
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

=   case _                                             => (0, t"")
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
